== the refusal path: terminal ended, no CLAUDE_EXIT line
   dispatch: launched in Orca terminal term_stub — "title"
dispatch: terminal term_stub ended without an CLAUDE_EXIT line — the launch did not complete honestly
|2
PASS refusal is reported as a launch failure (exit 2), not a result
== and dispatch never reaches the result writer on that path
   800:  orca_launch "$selector" "$title" "$command_text" "$exit_marker" "$LAUNCH_TIMEOUT"
   859:    '{story:$story, cycle:($cycle|tonumber), status:$status,
   (orca_launch dies before the jq that writes ${STORY}.result.json — die() exits)
== CONTROL: the same probe DOES harvest a real exit line
   dispatch: launched in Orca terminal term_stub — "title"
dispatch: CLAUDE_EXIT=0
|0
PASS control: a real CLAUDE_EXIT line is harvested (exit 0)
== the OTHER shape a real terminal may take: it outlives the command
   dispatch: launched in Orca terminal term_stub — "title"
dispatch: no CLAUDE_EXIT line after 3s — giving up rather than guessing the outcome
|2
NOTE still fail-closed, but only after the full launch timeout elapses
